<p>
  I had a paid subscription to Codecademy for a few years. I'm not trying to say that right now I'm fluent and proficient in all these areas, but I did do the course material and understood it at the time I was going through it. A lot of being a developer isn't knowing everything, it's being able to learn and figure stuff out as you go when challenges arise.
</p>
<p>
  That said, for me, I consider having these a personal accomplishment that I am proud of. I finished the main Front End and Full Stack Engineer ones early in 2026 and then I decided to let my subscription expire. So I then went on a binge of some of the individual courses which required the subscription before it expired.
</p>
<p>
   Aside from asking a debugging question here and there, I do not use A.I., I write all my code from scratch, and I enjoy every minute of it. This page will be about sharing some of the things I have built since I started my coding journey.
</p>

<script>
  // on desktop, with the decorative curtain border, it was hard to see the scrollbar
  // i wanted it to be draggable like a touchscreen
  const scroller = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".codecademy-certs-inner-wrapper");
  let isDown = false;
  let startX: number = 0;
  let scrollLeft: number = 0;

  scroller?.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    isDown = true;
    scroller.classList.add('active');
    startX = e.pageX;
    scrollLeft = scroller.scrollLeft;
  });

  const stopDragging = () => {
    if (!isDown) return;
    isDown = false;
    scroller?.classList.remove('active');
  };

  scroller?.addEventListener('mouseleave', stopDragging);
  scroller?.addEventListener('mouseup', stopDragging);

  scroller?.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
    if (!isDown) return;
    const walk = (e.pageX - startX);   
    scroller.scrollLeft = scrollLeft - walk;
  });

</script>

<style>
  p {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block: 2rem;
  }
  .certs-img-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-around;
    margin-block-start: 3rem;

    > img {
      @media (max-width: 500px) {
        width: 100%;
      }
    }

    img {
      display: block;
      max-width: 350px;
      height: auto;
      max-height: 100%;
    }
  }

  .codecademy-certs-outer-wrapper {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 65%;

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      max-width: 100%;
    }

  }
  .pseudo-anchor {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }
  .pseudo-anchor::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 998;
    pointer-events: none;
    inset: -0.5rem;

    background-image: url("/images/curtain-l-side.webp");
    background-size: 44rem 100%;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    
    /* using the equivalent bg image for the right side
      would not respond correctly as the screen got smaller,
      so i did a second left and flipped it, holy shit, it worked! */
    transform: scalex(-1);
    
  }

  .codecademy-certs-inner-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    overflow-x: scroll;
    position: relative;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    max-width: 725px;
    border-radius: 25px 25px 45px 45px;
    cursor: grab;
    outline: none;

    &:focus-visible {
      outline: 1px solid var(--text-color-700);
      outline-offset: 20px;
    }

    /* hide the scrollbar now that its draggable
    ffox/chrome, safari, edge */
    scrollbar-width: none; /* Firefox */
    &::-webkit-scrollbar {
      display: none; /* Chrome, Safari, newer Edge */
    }


    .cc-image-wrapper {
      min-width: 300px;
      max-height: 260px;
      scroll-snap-align: center;
      padding-block-start: 0.5rem;

      img {
        max-width: 100%;
        user-select: none;
        
      }

      &:first-child {
        padding-inline-start: 2rem;
      }
      &:last-child {
        padding-inline-end: 2rem;
      }

      @media (max-width: 500px) {
        min-width: 225px;
        max-height: 195px;
      }
    }
    &.active {
      cursor: grabbing;
      /* Prevents snap-fighting while dragging */
      scroll-snap-type: none;
      scroll-behavior: auto;
    }
  }

  .codecademy-certs-outer-wrapper::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 999;
    pointer-events: none;
    background-image: url("/images/curtain-top.webp");
    inset: -0.5rem;
    background-size: 100% 100%;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  .codecademy-certs-outer-wrapper::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 998;
    pointer-events: none;
    inset: -0.5rem;

    background-image: url("/images/curtain-l-side.webp");
    background-size: 44rem 100%;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;

    
  }
</style>
